MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because I want more of Clapton's relaxed, bluesy playing.",
    "Step Back connects with what draws me to Hendrix: expressive blues guitar. Revelator, Rhythm & Blues, and Slipstream also fit that interest in soulful playing."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "New's pop-oriented direction does not fit my appetite for blues guitar today, even though I also listen to melodic songwriting.",
    "Time gives me too little recognizable connection to my recent listening to motivate a choice; that uncertainty does not mean I dislike the music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in You Should Be So Lucky seems to have been stretched into a broader interest in singer-songwriters, while Ryan Adams and Standing in the Breach are less compelling to me today than the blues selections.",
    "Sharing a broad rootsy or classic-rock connection with my listening is not enough to make every album equally appealing right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Today I care most about the relaxed blues feel of Old Sock and the expressive guitar playing I associate with Hendrix.",
    "I rarely choose many albums at once. Passing on A Fool To Care or Slipstream reflects my narrow focus today, even though their soulful sound appeals to me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in soulful roots music, but my choices today favor blues guitar over the broader singer-songwriter connections."
}
